      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "The linear term in a sufficiently small conjugation yields a nontrivial perturbation character for each matrix in a large shell. Its quadratic error lies in the additive character kernel. Invariance of the index and Gram transform permits averaging before integrating in b. Absolute convergence has its own geometric shell estimate.",
      "review": "Checked the signs and the exponent, the independence of the cancellation cutoff from z, and the compact integral giving the entire function. Independently reviewed the finite-place hypotheses and the distinction between absolute convergence and continuation."
