    {
      "id": "EWH-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "At the special point the shrinking annihilator recovers the density",
      "anchor": "lifts-exceptional-value",
      "statement": "At s₀=(M−n)/2 the weight is 1. The integral over a sufficiently large b-ball equals the average of the Gram density on the translate by T of its annihilator. Continuity and self-dual volume normalization identify the stabilized integral with g(T).",
      "hypotheses": "Use the preceding local data and a continuous density g of the Φ-weighted Gram pushforward on the invertible locus, satisfying the measure identity on its compact subsets. In the example use 3 inert in ℚ(i), the conductor ℤ₃, J=I₂, n=1, T=1, equal integral lattices and the indicator of (1,0) mod 3.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-exceptional-average",
        "lifts-exceptional-three"
      ],
